$DIR/main.p:6:7: packed field type string must be an integer, bool, float, packed type or array of those
    A field of a packed type must have a fixed bit layout: an integer, bool,
    float, packed type, or an array of those. Strings, slices, pointers and
    structs have no fixed layout in bits.
    (see "packed types" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.14)
    (run "pluto explain E2104" for a longer explanation)
